  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 206 AM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nUnsettled weather will continue along and ahead of slow moving \ncold front today and tonight. Chances by daybreak will be 75-95%\nacross the northern two thirds of the PAH forecast area, with \nscattered to numerous showers and storms expected across the \nentire PAH fa through the day. By this evening, the best chances\n(40-70%) will become focused across the southern half of our \nregion, with southwest Indiana and portions of southern Illinois\nnorth of Route 13 dry late tonight. On Friday, 20-50% chances \nwill linger across our entire area, especially in the afternoon \ninto the evening, with the frontal boundary hanging up just \nsouth of our region and an upper trof moving over the region. \nThe front will lift back north late Friday night, keeping things\nunsettled into Saturday and Saturday evening, with isolated to \nscattered (20-50% chances) showers and storms possible.\n\nSPC Day 1 shows a Marginal Risk across the southeastern two-\nthirds of our region. The main concern with storms will continue\nto be damaging winds, primarily this afternoon into this evening.\n\nThe model blend keeps Sunday through Tuesday morning dry. By \nlate Tuesday into Tuesday night, models vary on the timing and \nlocation of a cold front moving into the central U.S. For now, \nthe model blend produces 20-50% chances of showers and storms \nTuesday afternoon through Wednesday.\n\nA big drop in temperatures can be expected today, with highs ranging \nfrom the middle 80s north to the lower 90s south.  Friday will see \nnear seasonal temperatures in the middle to upper 80s. The return of \nsoutherly winds over the weekend will result in a quick return of \nunseasonably warm conditions, with both highs and lows 5 to 8 \ndegrees above normal Saturday into the first half of next week.",
